Z||000012||Shiner||12-14-1999||11:47 AM||||ATI is just a brand of card, MonkeyMan.  I can highly recommend Adobe Photoshop.  It is not an extremely simple program, and it will take awhile to learn how to make things look the way  you want them, but you can do ANYTHING you want!  I recently touched up a photo of a GT with a stuck headlight motor, and now you wouldn't be able to tell from the pic that it was stuck up.  And, uh, I certainly didn't BUY this program.... That's all I'm gonna say..||||reg||1
Z||000013||Voyd||12-14-1999||01:13 PM||||find someone who has it, and "borrow" it. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||DaRkLoRD||12-14-1999||02:01 PM||||Paint Shop Pro would most likely be adequate for any editing you have to do, and some people use it for professional graphic design. <P>You can even use the shareware version indefinitely, but you have to put up with the nag screen when it starts up. The newer versions might actually stop working after 30 days, but at school last year we had one that was on day 520 of 30.. but I'm sure there are some benefits to registering.. just can't think of any besides getting rid of the nag screen..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 12-14-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Racer 1||12-14-1999||02:10 PM||||Heres my dream fiero racing.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=159982&a=1168563&p=14406672&Sequence=4"> ||||reg||10
Z||000016||Patrick||12-14-1999||03:50 PM||||<BR>When I bought my Epson Stylus 400 printer, it came with <B>Adobe PhotoDeluxe</B> thrown in as a bonus. I LOVE this program. I actually have a copy of Adobe Photoshop which I never use because it's way more complicated than what I need. I am able to do anything I want with <B>PhotoDeluxe</B>. It is NOT too basic. I also like the fact that the viewing window is quite large. Some photo programs force you to work within a relatively small area. The interface is also very straightforward and easy to understand.<P><B>Adobe PhotoDeluxe</B> is inexpensive (if you have to buy it) but very good. I give it two thumbs up! ||||reg||14
